[Fix] Security: safe_source() applied to all sourced files; state file
      operations wrapped in flock; mktemp replaces PID-based temp files;
      tlog gunzip/gzip race replaced with zcat
[Fix] Security: reject group-writable files in addition to world-writable
      in file safety checks; sanitize credential patterns in alert email
      log excerpts; validate IGNOREREGEX patterns before use
[Fix] Global lock: FD-based flock replaced with mkdir-based lock eliminating
      eval and fd-0-close risk; PID liveness check clears dead holder
      immediately for cron recovery
[Fix] Watch mode: SIGTERM/SIGINT now properly exit the daemon; previous trap
      pattern let the while-true loop continue after cleanup
[Fix] Watch mode reload: unset config vars BEFORE re-sourcing to prevent
      stale values; clear pressure arrays; re-register journal filters on
      SIGHUP; re-derive log format variables; add fallback variable block
      for config-sourcing failures; pre-validate syntax and permissions
      before unsetting to prevent degraded daemon state
[Fix] Watch mode reload: config validation uses return instead of exit,
      preventing daemon crash on validation errors
[Fix] Upgrade path: importconf preserves pressure-country.conf, custom rule
